payload:
  id: update-nexus
  repoUuid: null
  name: Update Nexus from GitHub
  about: >-
    James, 2026-11-01, after updating by hand (git branch --set-upstream-to, git pull, type VERSION,
    start:all): "can you make that a macro or framework and then into a command like a batch". What
    is newer, his yes, the update, then the version it left. Restarting what changed is still the
    Updates page (no command row restarts a system yet).
  steps:
    - tool: nexus.command
      args:
        command: update
    - confirm: >-
        Bring in the newer Nexus from GitHub (fast-forward only; your changed data files are copied
        aside first)
    - tool: nexus.command
      args:
        command: update apply
        flags:
          'yes': true
    - tool: nexus.command
      args:
        command: system version
    - check:
        of: 4
        matches: Nexus \d+\.\d+\.\d+
  from:
    kind: library
  runs: []
  runCount: 0
  createdAt: 1793577600000
  updatedAt: 1793577600000
